    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18008" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐτό-φῠτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>self-engendered</i>:
			hence, <i>arising naturally,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕλκεα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					3.47
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Antipho Trag.
			</span></i> ap. <i>Lex.Sabb.; native,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρετή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.C.
					44.37
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>natural, primitive,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐργασία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1256a40
				</span></i>
			.</div>
